82:| Exact | HLG footage over BT.2020, PQ up to 1,000 cd/m², footage with a built-in Camera Log except at its very brightest highlights, and SDR material |
83:| Close, not exact | HLG footage over P3 or BT.709 primaries, PQ highlights above 1,000 cd/m², and a key picked on a gain-map photo |
hdr-source-conversion | one-conversion-at-the-start | Each frame of a source is converted once, at the very start of the picture pipeline, into the project's working colour, so most footage needs no setting.
hdr-source-rec709 | rec-709-and-untagged-sources | Ordinary Rec. 709 or untagged video, stills and recordings are drawn as they are in an SDR project and lifted to HDR reference white in an HDR (HLG) project, so they look the same.
hdr-source-hlg | hlg-video | HLG video such as iPhone HDR is converted to Rec. 709 with its highlights rolled off smoothly in an SDR project, and kept as HLG with its highlights above white intact in an HDR (HLG) project.
hdr-source-pq | pq-and-hdr10-video | A PQ (HDR10) file is converted to Rec. 709 with its highlights rolled off at the file's own peak in an SDR project, and becomes real HDR in an HDR (HLG) project.
hdr-source-wide-gamut | wide-gamut-sdr | A source with BT.2020 or P3 D65 primaries and an SDR transfer (sRGB included) is converted to the project's colours rather than drawn with the wrong ones.
hdr-source-srgb | srgb-transfer-files | A source labelled with the sRGB transfer is read as sRGB rather than as Rec. 709.
hdr-source-full-range | full-range-files | S-Log3 and V-Log files stored in full range are read as full range, from the flag in the file.
hdr-source-camera-log | camera-log | Footage with a Camera Log set becomes a normal-looking Rec. 709 picture in an SDR project and real HDR in an HDR (HLG) project.
hdr-source-hdr-stills | hdr-stills | A still labelled HLG or PQ is treated as HDR, the way a video of the same transfer is, rather than being read as SDR.
hdr-source-gain-map | gain-map-photos | An iPhone HDR photo with a gain map (HEIC) shows its HDR highlights in an HDR (HLG) project and its ordinary picture in an SDR project.
hdr-same-everywhere | the-same-everywhere | The source conversion works the same way in the preview, every export, rendered and saved frames, the timeline's filmstrip and the Media tab's thumbnails.
camera-log-detection | detection-on-import | An iPhone Apple Log or Apple Log 2 file is recognised by its label when you import it, so it looks like normal video straight away.

